WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:06.740
okay. As many of you know, I am not a socialist.
I am a social Democrat. That probably doesn't

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.840
come as a shock to people who have been watching
this show or listening to the show for a while.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.070
Social Democrats are capitalism lists

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:22.320
in the sense that we are not trying to overthrow
capitalism and replace it with socialism or

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.971
Marxism or communism or some system in which,
uh, there's no more private property, private

00:00:28.971 --> 00:00:36.059
businesses, et cetera. We recognize the many,
many, many failings of capitalism, but we

00:00:36.059 --> 00:00:43.230
want to fix them. And one of the reasons that
capitalism has to be fixed is that it doesn't

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:49.309
work for tons of people, but the interesting
thing about this is that if you want some

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:55.989
form of capitalism to remain, you had better
damn well fix it because the longer and longer

00:00:55.989 --> 00:01:01.479
it goes without working for millions and millions
and millions of people, it makes the system

00:01:01.479 --> 00:01:08.940
more at risk of being overthrown by some other
system. This was the concept in fact of Marxism

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:14.020
that eventually there would be this uprising
of the proletariat that would take down the

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.770
bourgeoisie. Of course it has not happened
in the United States, but the worst capitalism

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.540
is the more likely that that becomes.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:25.310
That gets us to today's sort of news, which
is that case in point, there's a new poll

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:32.090
which says seven out of 10 millennials would
vote for a socialist candidate. I do wonder

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:37.250
whether the people responding to the poll
actually know what socialism is because it

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:42.020
seems like lots of people talk about socialism
and they don't actually know what it is, but

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:46.050
let's assume for a second just for the sake
of discussion because the analysis is still

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:52.030
an interesting one. This poll was released
yesterday. It finds 70% of millennials are

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:57.530
either somewhat or extremely likely to vote
for a socialist political candidate. 50% of

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:03.850
millennials have a somewhat or very unfavorable
view of capitalism which is up from last year.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:11.720
Overall capitalism is still viewed more favorably
than other economic systems, 61% positive,

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:17.410
but this is a very clear trend line even if
many of these people are mixing up socialism

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.050
and social democracy.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:26.780
The trend line is clear and this is why social
Democrats who are for better regulated social

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:33.200
capitalism need to fix capitalism and by the
way, not that I'm in the vulture capitalist

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.610
free market, laissez Faire type of camp. If
you're a VAR, vulture capitalist and you want

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:44.740
to keep some form of capitalism, this should
be a wake up call for you as well. This is

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:50.910
why you need to be fixing capitalism with
the socially democratic reforms that people

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:56.600
on the left of the democratic party have been
talking about for many years. The least damaging

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:04.930
thing to a capitalist is to fix capitalism
or they risk some other system actually, uh,

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:08.450
becoming something people really and truly
want. You know, when Donald Trump says during

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:13.880
his state of the union, we will never be a
Capitol, a socialist country. Uh, he doesn't

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.680
know that. As I've said before, things change
in countries.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.920
They can change slowly, they can change more
quickly than sometimes we believe is possible.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:26.830
Uh, but the reality is that there's no real
risk right now of the U S becoming actually

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:32.590
socialist. You know, college tuition paid
through taxes is not socialism. A Medicare

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:39.349
for all isn't socialism, gun controls, not
socialism, but the right has both successfully

00:03:39.349 --> 00:03:47.310
and unsuccessfully used the term socialism
as an argument to attack these socially democratic

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:52.170
policies. But eventually there's going to
have to be some accounting because as capitalism,

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:58.629
as we know, it continues to fail more and
more people and fail to provide a basic standard

00:03:58.629 --> 00:04:04.849
of living and allow these just sickening excesses
of wealth to accumulate more and more and

00:04:04.849 --> 00:04:09.780
more at the top. Millennials who see that
system is failing them. Why wouldn't they

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:15.930
be open to some other system? They don't see
all of the great things that capitalism is

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:21.140
bringing them because it's arguably not brought
them a lot of great things.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:24.830
So of course they're going to look at something
else because our version of capitalism is

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:29.360
fundamentally broken. So if you really want
to tout the benefits of capitalism, and by

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.490
this I mean some of the main tenants, right?
Private property, private business ownership,

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:39.160
uh, taxation, which tends to be progressive
taxation. Although, you know, different people

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:42.860
argue about how progressive it should be.
Lots of the things that we have. If you want

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:47.930
to really make the case that it's working,
you've got to make it work for more people.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:52.889
And that includes making sure no one drops
below a certain standard of living. That includes

00:04:52.889 --> 00:04:58.750
cutting down on the corrosive influence of
money in politics and an influence peddling.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:05.110
The data is increasingly clear on this. Something
will have to be done or other systems, even

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:09.590
misunderstood systems, and this is why I said
you know, a lot of people don't know the different,

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:12.330
don't realize what socialism actually is.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:16.730
It doesn't matter because no matter what your
assessment is of what capitalism is and what

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:21.830
socialism is, if people understand that the
system as it exists is not working for them,

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:24.162
it becomes harder and harder to argue that
this is the system that we should keep

